  "response_text": "You would simply start the same way as before by subtracting from MSP_init_val to find the PSP value, then from the PSP value you would subtract the amount of memory needed for the next stack and put a PSP for the next stack there. This is repeated as many times as is necessary throughout memory until all stacks have been initialized. Note that in order for this to work that the memory has to be large enough to allow for all of the memory to be allocated in this way. You also need to ensure that each stack starts at a proper value, which is a multiple of 8 bytes.\\n",
